+# Umami migration preparation
+
+This checkout starts at upstream tag `v3.0.3`. The source VPS also runs Umami
+3.0.3 and PostgreSQL 16. Keep this application version for the database move.
+The Netlify project is `tgb-umami` (`834e8e23-92fd-4c79-9da5-d7d068df5ed7`).
+It is separate from the main Tahiti Guest Boat website.
+
+## Local prerequisites and deployment
+
+Use an official Node 22 installation with pnpm 11.25.0. The Node binary bundled
+with ChatGPT enforces macOS library validation and cannot load the Rollup/SWC
+native modules. A verified official Node runtime is available locally under
+`/Users/leo/.local/share/tgb-umami/runtime/`; `active-node.json` records its bin
+directory and archive checksum. Put that bin directory first in PATH.
+
+The ignored `.env` contains the pooled Neon URL, original APP_SECRET, and a
+direct URL for explicit migration operations. It is mode 600. `.netlify` is
+also ignored; its state file links only this Umami project. Runtime credentials
+live in Netlify variables, marked secret. Never put them in `netlify.toml` or
+client-prefixed variables.
+
+From the checkout root:
+
+```sh
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm --package=netlify-cli dlx netlify status
+bash ops/deploy-preview.sh
+```
+
+`DOTENV_CONFIG_OVERRIDE` is for local builds: it lets the private local `.env`
+override masked write-only values returned by Netlify. Do not set it as a
+Netlify runtime variable. Build-time migrations are disabled deliberately;
+schema changes must use the direct Neon endpoint in a separate explicit step.
+
+The tested script runs build and deploy together: the Next.js adapter temporarily
+places public assets in the publish directory and restores the internal build
+directory afterwards. An independent `netlify deploy --no-build` using `.next`
+therefore misses public assets and can publish server build files. If separating
+the commands, use `.netlify/static` after a fully successful Netlify build and
+retain its generated functions and routing metadata. Do not combine `--context`
+with `--no-build`; the CLI rejects that pair. The script creates a draft. It does
+not publish the primary site or change DNS.
+
+Validated preview: https://migration-check--tgb-umami.netlify.app, deploy
+`6b0227c50839c6cd84df7b7f`. Heartbeat, tracker, login and authenticated historical
+statistics passed. The API reports the same pageview totals as PostgreSQL:
+3,115 for Tahiti Guest Boat and 97,501 for Yamaha TMMB.
+
+The smoke check uses a five-minute admin token in memory, derived from the
+preserved APP_SECRET, to read the restored statistics. It does not change users,
+passwords, websites, or analytics events.
+
+## Backup and restore
+
+The private backup directory is
+`/Users/leo/Backups/TahitiGuestBoat/umami/2026-11-21`.
+It contains a custom-format dump, SHA-256 manifest, catalogue, source Docker
+configuration, Coolify compose/environment archive, connection settings, and
+verification results. These files contain private data and must stay outside Git.
+
+Use `python3 ops/migrate-db.py --help` for the reusable CLI. Supply the private
+`source-context.json`, SSH key, and a new timestamped archive path. The backup
+operation streams `pg_dump` out of the existing PostgreSQL 16 container, verifies
+the archive catalogue, and refuses to overwrite an existing backup. It leaves
+the application running.
+
+For restore, provide `--connection-file` pointing to private JSON with the direct
+Neon URL under `direct`. The script rejects pooled endpoints and nonempty target
+databases. It restores in one transaction without resetting or dropping a
+database. Both operations require the source VPS only as a PostgreSQL client;
+after its expiry, the archive can instead be restored using any PostgreSQL 16+
+`pg_restore` client and a private libpq service configuration:
+
+```sh
+PGSERVICE=umami_direct pg_restore --dbname service=umami_direct \
+  --no-owner --no-acl --exit-on-error --single-transaction /absolute/path/umami.dump
+```
+
+## Final cutover: still pending
+
+Hostinger is still the live collector. The Neon database is a validated copy at
+2026-11-21 23:03 UTC; newer source activity is not included yet.
+
+1. Verify the working preview and keep the current VPS subscription unchanged.
+2. Prepare a new empty Neon database for the final snapshot, avoiding destructive
+   replacement of the validated copy. Retain the same PostgreSQL/application versions,
+   APP_SECRET, website IDs, accounts, reports, and segments.
+3. Arrange a brief collection maintenance window; pause the old application,
+   take a final backup, restore it, and compare counts and table fingerprints.
+   Requests during this brief pause may be missed; do not promise zero downtime.
+4. Configure both the old collector and Netlify to use that final Neon database.
+   Persist the old service environment through Coolify/Compose. Start and test
+   the old collector again before moving DNS, so clients with cached DNS still
+   write to the same database. Keep its original local database intact.
+5. Publish a **new** production deploy, attach `analytics.tahitiguestboat.com`,
+   complete the certificate setup, and update only that hostname's DNS.
+6. Verify tracker loading, collection, statistics, and TLS through the custom
+   domain. Check both endpoints during DNS propagation. Retain backups and the
+   source until verification completes; remove temporary access afterwards.
+
+Do not run a destructive restore over the live Neon database. Do not switch DNS
+to an untested application or leave the two collectors writing to separate
+databases. The current scope is preparation; this cutover has not been executed.
