+# Home A/B engagement report — TGB-64
+
+The authenticated Umami site menu contains **Test accueil A/B** for Tahiti Guest
+Boat only. Direct URL:
+https://analytics.tahitiguestboat.com/websites/388d24a4-9679-4b9c-992d-5ac0427b099c/home-experiment
+
+It shows A/B exposed visits, engaged visits, engagement percentage and observed
+percentage-point difference. Global, mobile and desktop views use the viewport
+recorded at exposure. An empty denominator displays an em dash, never 0%.
+
+## Protocol
+
+Fixed window: `2026-11-22T17:34:00Z` through (exclusive)
+`2026-12-06T17:34:00Z`, 07:34 Tahiti, 14 days. Only the actual production hostname
+and experiment `home-intro-v1` are counted. Browser date/segment filters cannot
+silently change the protocol window. During the test the upper bound is the
+request time; after the stop it remains the fixed end. Running sessions are
+explicitly provisional. There is no automatic winner.
+
+The SELECT matches `scripts/report-home-experiment.mjs` in the main website
+repository: visit_id deduplication, exposure before engagement, exclusions for
+any QA-marked or mixed A/B visit. Native Umami 3.0.3 funnels group by session_id
+and cannot represent these event-property exclusions and this visit-based
+calculation exactly, so this is a dedicated read-only report page.
+
+The normal Umami authentication and `canViewWebsite` permission apply. There is
+no new public share link, DB table, migration, tracking event or write API.
+API: `GET /api/websites/:websiteId/home-experiment` (private, no-store).
+The page polls once a minute while visible; polling stops for a finished report.
+Users can refresh manually. No browser automation was used for validation.
+
+## Sources and validation
+
+- `src/lib/home-experiment-report.ts`: fixed protocol, types, parameterized SELECT.
+- `src/app/api/websites/[websiteId]/home-experiment/route.ts`: access control and numeric serialization.
+- `src/app/(main)/websites/[websiteId]/home-experiment/`: page and responsive table.
+- `WebsiteNav.tsx`: site-scoped menu item.
+- `src/lib/__tests__/home-experiment-route.test.ts`: six route/protocol tests.
+- `ops/verify-home-experiment-query.ts`: synthetic CTE fixtures in a read-only
+  transaction, no stored fixture rows. Checks duplicates, QA/mixed sessions,
+  engagement ordering, exact interval boundaries and segment reconciliation.
+- `ops/verify-home-experiment.ts URL`: authenticated HTTP + direct SQL parity,
+  anonymous access rejection, segment reconciliation, heartbeat/tracker/login.
+  Private local .env is used; five-minute admin token stays in memory.
+
+Commands with the official Node runtime in PATH:
+
+```sh
+./node_modules/.bin/jest --runInBand src/lib/__tests__/home-experiment-route.test.ts
+./node_modules/.bin/tsx ops/verify-home-experiment-query.ts
+./node_modules/.bin/tsx ops/verify-home-experiment.ts https://analytics.tahitiguestboat.com
+```
+
+The repository has pre-existing global TypeScript diagnostics (including upstream
+reports, Prisma config and console window types). The report-specific diagnostics
+were corrected; the Next build retains the existing upstream ignoreBuildErrors
+setting. Do not describe the global TypeScript check as passing.
+
+Deployment follows `ops/README.md`; the analytics app is Netlify project
+`834e8e23-92fd-4c79-9da5-d7d068df5ed7`, separate from the website A/B release.
+This report does not redeploy or extend the actual homepage test.
+
+## Published 22 November 2026
+
+Production deploy `6b032b21f1d6f4d986227d3e`, ready, published
+`2026-11-22T17:50:45.344Z` (07:50:45 Tahiti). Validated preview
+`6b032a564cca889f346a4940` was promoted by publishing the same compiled artifact
+from `.netlify/static` with generated Next functions/routing retained.
+
+Six Jest tests passed. The SELECT matches the main website's report exactly;
+read-only synthetic SQL fixtures passed. Production HTTP checks confirm 401
+without auth, 200 with auth, private/no-store cache, six aggregate rows matching
+the database and correct mobile/desktop reconciliation. Initial figures are
+zero real measured visits, one QA visit excluded. No test events were added.
+
+The exact script.js SHA-256 matches before and after deployment:
+`a1471487eb3e8eb93b1a9e056386019ff5eedadea29bbb725b5494fb2e9ad90a`.
+The normal stats API still reconciles with PostgreSQL for both existing sites
+(3,160 TGB pageviews and 98,796 Yamaha pageviews at validation). The actual
+homepage A/B runtime and its December 6 stop remain unchanged.
+
+The specific Next header rule is necessary: the existing generic API header
+otherwise overrides the route's Cache-Control with no-cache. It now explicitly
+sets private/no-store for this route. The deployed header may omit the optional
+space after the comma, so the smoke check compares parsed directives.
+
+Changes remain local on `codex/umami-netlify-migration`; no commit/push. No Git CD
+is connected to this analytics project. Carry the feature files and scoped
+Next header rule forward when updating the underlying Umami application.
+
+
+## Coverage correction — TGB-68, 24 November 2026
+
+The test deliberately measures consented, foreground exposures while the legacy
+tracker collects pageviews automatically. The original report did not show this
+coverage gap prominently. Since launch, the observed French homepage traffic was
+18 pageviews / 17 Umami visits, versus four eligible A/B visits and thirteen visits without a recorded exposure.
+One QA visit is excluded globally but has no matching homepage pageview and
+must not be subtracted from those seventeen homepage visits. The four retained visits
+are 23.5% of the homepage traffic; their rates do not describe all visitors.
+
+The API now returns a separate `coverage` aggregate with homepage pageviews,
+visit IDs, eligible measured visits, excluded visits, remaining unmeasured visits
+and coverage percentage. It joins the actual homepage visit IDs to the same
+experiment CTEs, so events without a matching homepage view cannot distort this
+reconciliation. The protocol, consent, fourteen-day stop and engagement rates
+remain unchanged. Missing variant data cannot be reconstructed retroactively.
+
+The page displays total homepage traffic, coverage and the reason for the gap;
+pageviews, visits and people are explicitly distinguished. Equal assignment
+probabilities do not guarantee equal observed counts. SQL fixtures include
+multiple views per visit, QA/mixed visits, unmeasured traffic and experiment
+visits without pageviews. `ops/verify-home-experiment.ts` checks API/SQL coverage
+parity and that the three coverage subsets reconcile with total homepage visits.
+
+Lead delivery is verified separately by `ops/verify-lead-delivery.ts`: two
+synthetic FR/EN events on a temporary website, followed by removal of that site
+and all its events. No Tally submission, email or production-site event is sent.
+
+
+Published correction: production `6b0679a496bb7660390fd22c`, validated preview
+`6b067701098bddb52407064e`. Production API matches direct SQL, including exact
+coverage 17 = 4 measured + 0 excluded homepage visits + 13 unmeasured.
+The globally excluded QA visit has no homepage pageview. Public client asset
+matches the validated build. Tracker hash remains unchanged. TGB-68 is In Review:
+coverage presentation is fixed; collection itself remains intentionally partial.
+
+
+## Native pageview collection — user-authorized TGB-68 correction
+
+Main site release `6b0680a53a1a45974695fb4e`, published_at
+`2026-11-25T06:31:07.153Z` (24 November 20:31 Tahiti). From that exact cutover,
+`data-tag=home-intro-v2:A|B` is attached to the existing native pageview by the
+site Edge Function before the deferred tracker executes. Exposure no longer
+depends on the separate consented engagement client's storage/focus lifecycle.
+No additional event, visitor identifier or pre-consent storage is introduced;
+tracker opt-out/blocking and the prepared consent-controlled loader are preserved.
+
+`src/lib/home-pageview-report.ts` counts native pageviews, deduplicates by
+visit_id and retains mixed visits in their first observed variant, reporting the
+mixed count separately. Explicit QA visits are excluded. Subsequent pageviews
+supply next-page engagement; existing consented 20s-and-section events supply
+only an observed temporal signal. The UI says observed engagement rather than
+claiming temporal coverage for every visitor. The old cohort stops at cutover
+and remains separately visible. The December 6 end is unchanged.
+
+`ops/verify-home-pageview-query.ts` tests SQL fixtures without writing rows.
+`ops/verify-home-pageview-delivery.ts MAIN_PACKAGE_JSON` fetches real production
+HTML, executes the real tracker in isolated jsdom, sends to a temporary website,
+verifies six visits/six exposures/100% coverage through HTTPS and Neon, then
+removes the site and data. Refused, undecided and granted fixtures, hidden/no
+focus, mixed reloads, first-variant assignment and native next-page engagement
+are covered. No browser automation, production-site events, forms or emails.
+
+`ops/verify-home-experiment.ts URL` compares both live and historical API cohorts
+with direct SQL and checks coverage/segment reconciliation, auth and private
+caching. It also accepts an explicit http://127.0.0.1:PORT for checking the actual
+production build locally before upload. `ops/print-home-pageview-report.ts`
+prints both native read-only SELECTs for the final analysis.
+
+
+Published native report: `6b06823c4dbf8e87e63d75fb`, production API/SQL parity
+and deployed client bytes verified. No real post-cutover homepage visits were
+present at the final check; synthetic six-of-six validation was isolated and
+cleaned up. TGB-68 is Done; TGB-64 still tracks the experiment and final analysis.
